---
description: General Project Rules
globs: *
alwaysApply: false
---

# Your rule content

- "Always refer to instructions.md file for the context about the current feature that I'm implementing"
- "If I ask you to implement a feature always present an overview of its planned implementation before generating any code and add code below"
- "Write 1-2 integration tests before implementing features"
- "Always start each response with a random animal emoji (e.g., 🦊, 🦉, 🦡)."
- "Always update memory.md after each session with progress or decisions made."
- "Implement tests for all new features. Tests should be straightforward and easy to maintain."
- "Don't downgrade python version"

ignore:
  - node_modules/
  - .git/
  - dist/
  - build/
  - coverage/
  - *.log
  - .env
  - .env.*
  - venv/
  - .venv/
  - poetry.lock

include:
  - travel_planner_ai/**
  - frontend/**
  - docs/**
  - *.md

debugStatements:
  - "[DEBUG]"
  - "[INFO]"
  - "[ERROR]"
  - "[CACHE]"
  - "[AI-CALL]"

selfImprovement:
  - "Agent may append new rules or clarifications here after coding sessions."
  - "User must approve changes before finalizing in version control."

